{% tool-context
   title="Bandwidth Calculator"
   question="What is bandwidth planning?"
   definition="Bandwidth planning turns request demand and payload size into a link-capacity decision. It protects latency during peaks while making compression, headroom, transfer windows, and cost assumptions explicit."
   inputs="Model requests per second, payload size, compression, protocol overhead, peak demand, target utilization, link capacity, and a scheduled bulk transfer."
   outcome="See average and peak throughput, monthly transfer, safe headroom, overload consequences, the next practical capacity tier, and an editable transfer-cost estimate."
   experiment="Inject a regional-failover challenge, then recover by changing compression, capacity, or the bulk-transfer window. The healthy state should return without hiding the formula that changed it." /%}

